ent-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:1b58a6c89a84de6913087931cdda614ab86cebfe6cd87cfd1a1ed750e4c904ec","file":"preprints/A-counterexample-to-Tachikawas-second-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":267,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"c5b4894bceafabeae116ba56c1e3c23c6afe9fc2a4e3256155f1393e86965129","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-counterexample-to-Tachikawas-second-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:1b58a6c89a84de6913087931cdda614ab86cebfe6cd87cfd1a1ed750e4c904ec","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-counterexample-to-Tachikawas-second-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L267"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:homological}\nLet $A,M$ be as in Theorem~\\ref{thm:main}. For every field extension\n$K/k$, put $A_K=K\\otimes_k A$, $M_K=K\\otimes_k M$, and\n\\[\n \\Gamma_K=\\End_{A_K}(A_K\\oplus M_K)^{\\mathrm{op}}.\n\\]\nThen $\\Gamma_K$ is a finite-dimensional $K$-algebra with the following\nproperties, in the category of finite left $\\Gamma_K$-modules.\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item Every term of the minimal injective resolution of $\\Gamma_K$\nis projective, but $\\idim_{\\Gamma_K}\\Gamma_K=\\infty$.\n\\item There is a nonzero simple module $S$ such that\n$\\Ext_{\\Gamma_K}^i(S,\\Gamma_K)=0$ for every $i\\geq0$.\n\\item There is a projective-injective Wakamatsu tilting module $W$\nwhich is not tilting.\n\\end{enumerate}\nConsequently the classical, generalized, and strong Nakayama conjectures,\nthe Auslander--Gorenstein conjecture, and the Wakamatsu tilting conjecture\nare false for finite-dimensional algebras over $K$."}
